    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d367">

                <pb facs="0688" n="592" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg592"/>

                <head>No. 365.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish to Mr. Bassett.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1873-11-01"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 1,
                        1873</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 170.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your dispatch No. 251, of the 15th ultimo,
                    has been received. It is gratifying to learn from it that the present
                    administration in Hayti <pb facs="0689" n="593" xml:id="pg593"/> shows a
                    disposition to provide for claims founded on contract which originated during
                    the administration of Salnave. If such a course should be adopted, it would
                    materially redound to the honor and strengthen the credit of the Haytian
                    government under all future administrations.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
